# Advanced Econometrics Project: The Geopolitics of Oil
## Macroeconomic Impact of the 2026 Gulf Crisis

## 📌 Project Overview
This repository contains the complete data pipeline, econometric analysis, and final report for the project **"The Geopolitics of Oil: Macroeconomic Impact of the 2026 Gulf Crisis."**

The study examines the macroeconomic effects of the oil price shock resulting from the 2026 Gulf Crisis on the three largest Eurozone economies: **Germany, France, and Italy**. Using monthly panel data from January 2023 to June 2026 (N = 126 observations; 3 countries × 42 months), the project employs Pooled OLS, Fixed Effects (FE), and Random Effects (RE) models to estimate the impact of oil price changes on consumer price inflation (CPI) and industrial production (IPI).

**Institution:** Tunis Business School (University of Tunis)  
**Course:** Advanced Econometrics - BA 351  
**Academic Year:** 2025 – 2026

